1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:27,270
I'm the Captain of Jianghai Team.

3
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:28,960
I want to report an issue.

4
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,220
We haven't paid the deposit for the next phase yet,

5
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,620
but why did our food quality suddenly drop?

6
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,540
Look, if you're not sleeping well,

7
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:38,940
you can skip morning practice the next day.

8
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:39,900
Thanks for your concern.

9
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,260
But I can't accept that.

10
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Episode 13

11
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:52,380
They're already arguing.

12
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,780
This is the perfect time to challenge Jacky.

13
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,170
Once he lost, he wouldn't dare act so arrogant anymore!

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,060
And now of all times,

15
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:01,980
I get blocked by a Coward on my own Team.

16
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,820
Leo was just looking out for the Team, you know.

17
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:09,270
Matthew was the one who stepped
up and provoked them first.

18
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:11,580
We're in the wrong here. Right?

19
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:16,860
No way. They started it by mocking us.

20
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,260
Why should we be the ones feeling guilty?

21
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,620
It was Matthew who went and provoked them first.

22
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,980
Yeah. That almost caused a huge mess.

23
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,380
If we'd actually gotten into a fight in the dining hall

24
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,540
and gotten kicked out,

25
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,740
we'd be in serious trouble.

26
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,580
I think it's safer to just listen to Coach.

27
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,980
Matthew, you're way too emotional.

28
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,300
I think even if Matthew was deliberately provoking them,

29
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,740
he was doing it for the Team's pride.

30
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:47,580
Still better than someone with no guts at all.

31
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,420
You all heard that, right?

32
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:28,860
Well?

33
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,780
Without Coach Sarah around to help you guys,

34
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,220
you're scared, huh?

35
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:35,100
I think you're the ones who are scared.

36
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,540
Your Coach isn't here,

37
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,910
and you're hiding from us like a bunch of Cowards.

38
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,860
Hiding from you? What a joke.

39
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,220
Our Captain came here today specifically to challenge you.

40
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:48,060
If you don't accept, then you're the real Cowards.

41
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,900
Ha! Our Captain's been waiting for this day.

42
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,820
I can barely wait any longer.

43
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:55,740
A promise is a promise.

44
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:57,660
There's no backing out now.

45
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,460
Captain! It's Jacky.

46
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,580
What's going on out there?

47
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:39,900
No clue.

48
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,300
The vibe feels kinda off, though.

49
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,140
Oh! Hey, Sis!

50
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,580
Sis, come check this out!

51
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,460
Look! Mark's about to face off against Jacky!

52
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,890
We gotta go cheer him on! Hurry up!

53
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,710
You actually showed up, huh?

54
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,620
Didn't you lose badly enough last year?

55
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,510
Well, things are different now.

56
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:01,980
Alright then, Let's go.

57
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:03,900
Everyone back up!

58
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:27,900
Coiling Dragon Tornado!

59
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:28,990
Golden Dragon Tail Whip!

60
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,260
Yeah!

61
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,700
Awesome! Beautiful!

62
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,580
Chengnan Team's no match for Jianghai Team.

63
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,620
This isn't over yet.

64
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:36,540
Now that was a sweet victory.

65
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:39,900
Let's see Jacky act all high and mighty tomorrow.

66
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:41,820
They've already quieted down a lot right now.

67
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,220
I think they already realize

68
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:45,660
their Captain lost to us.

69
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:50,940
They're probably drowning in sorrow right now.

70
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:52,860
Matthew!

71
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,150
Why'd she come here?

72
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:57,660
Matthew!

73
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,030
I brought you some bug spray and mosquito coils.

74
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,020
I brought them from home.

75
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,420
Figured you could use them.

76
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:07,260
Nah, I'm good. You keep them for yourself.

77
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,700
There aren't any mosquitoes in my cabin anyway.

78
00:09:09,710 --> 00:09:11,460
But they're perfect for you, aren't they?

79
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,900
Matthew, just take them.

80
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:19,260
We actually needed some anyway. Thanks.

81
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,220
No problem.

82
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,100
Later, Matthew!

83
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,780
Hmph. "There aren't any mosquitoes in my cabin."

84
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:33,180
She's obviously just showing
off how much better she's got it.

85
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,580
I think she was being really thoughtful.

86
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:39,420
She's always extra nice whenever she sees Matthew.

87
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,300
Think she might be a spy for Chengnan Team?

88
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,110
Why would we be scared of a spy?
We've got nothing to hide.

89
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,100
I mean, come on.

90
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,500
She was Matthew's Classmate back in Elementary School.

91
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,160
So does that mean they're childhood sweethearts?

92
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,520
Mickey, stop talking nonsense.

93
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:07,500
David

94
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:13,980
Meatball, come here!

95
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,460
Meatball! The Captain's got a sweet deal for you.

96
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:27,900
Stop messing with me.

97
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:30,300
For real.

98
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,700
Captain knows you've been getting

99
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,140
eaten alive by mosquitoes lately.

100
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,020
So he wants to make it up to you.

101
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:37,980
Is it food?

102
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,900
Obviously, dummy.

103
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:41,340
Is it a special breakfast?

104
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,490
Way better than that.

105
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,140
Come on, tell me already!

106
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,020
The Captain's sending you out today

107
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,940
to buy some supplies for the Team.

108
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,820
That way you can get whatever you want, no restrictions.

109
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,700
Captain, you understand me way too well!

110
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,140
Just keep it between us.

111
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:01,200
And you'll return the favour right?

112
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,460
No problem.

113
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,380
As long as the Captain writes down

114
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,910
exactly what he needs to buy,

115
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:08,700
I'll know what to do.
How hard could it be?

116
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,470
What I'm saying is, since the
Captain's being so good to you,

117
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,390
You should be a little nicer to the Captain too.

118
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,980
Of course I am.

119
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:18,780
Just remember that.

120
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:31,560
I'm nice to everyone.
What are they even talking about?

121
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:43,260
Monica, what's wrong?

122
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,660
My middle finger kinda hurts.

123
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:47,100
Think it's swollen?

124
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:49,020
It's not that serious.

125
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:49,980
You're probably just tired.

126
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,350
That's the finger you wear a ring on someday.

127
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,820
Gotta take good care of it.

128
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:55,940
Captain.

129
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,020
Monica, if your finger's bothering you,

130
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,460
you can take a break.

131
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:03,900
Thanks, Captain.

132
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:17,620
Monica! The Captain sent me to give you this finger sleeve.

133
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,140
Put it on later and your finger won't hurt as much.

134
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:24,060
The Captain's so thoughtful.

135
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,820
Actually, I'm the one who bought it.

136
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,670
So is from you, or from the Captain?

137
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,580
Either way works.

138
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,820
Come on over, fresh fruit!

139
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:47,110
Very cheap, very affordable!

140
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,990
How much for these bananas?

141
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:49,980
3 bucks.

142
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,390
Too much. What about these?

143
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:52,830
Not expensive, 5 bucks.

144
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:53,820
5 bucks for how much?

145
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,260
It's a great deal.

146
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,150
Not buying.

147
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,110
Come on, come on!

148
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,100
What about the apples?

149
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:00,510
2 bucks.

150
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:01,980
Why's everything so expensive here? Forget it.

151
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,380
Come back, I'll make it cheaper!

152
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,750
It's a bargain.

153
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,190
No deal. 2 bucks!

154
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,110
2.50!

155
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,030
Only 2 bucks.

156
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,980
Alright, alright. You little rascal.

157
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:15,900
1 bunch of bananas.

158
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:17,820
How much for the apples?

159
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:18,780
2 bucks a pound.

160
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,220
1.50!

161
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,140
1.80!

162
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,550
1.50!

163
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,980
Fine, fine. You little punk.

164
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,900
And he said this was a sweet gig.

165
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,270
I had to buy everything for the whole Team.

166
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,260
I'm wiped out.

167
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:34,140
Mark doesn't usually like chips that much.

168
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,580
I'll eat 'em.

169
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:51,420
Mickey might not even like bananas.

170
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,860
I'll try one for him.

171
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:08,700
I mean, I only bought a tiny bit of beef anyway.

172
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,620
I'll just finish it off.

173
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,060
And if they ask about it later,

174
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,980
I'll just say I didn't get any.

175
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,900
I doubt they'll even suspect anything.

176
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,340
Buying stuff for everyone,

177
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,700
and here you are sneaking food all alone.

178
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:38,940
That kind of behaviour isn't very nice, is it?

179
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:39,900
Who are you?

180
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,370
Who I am doesn't matter.

181
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,660
What matters is...

182
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,980
You're with Jianghai Team, right?

183
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:50,960
You think you can just say Jianghai Team's name like that?

184
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,220
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

185
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:03,420
This move's called "Feint East, Strike West."
Got it?

186
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:06,780
Using a Yo-Yo for something this low.

187
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:10,620
That's way over the line!
Give me back my banana peel!

188
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,020
Oh, so you like banana peels,

189
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,940
but you don't like playing with Yo-Yos?

190
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:17,340
Oh, so you're a fellow Yo-Yo Player.

191
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,260
If you wanted a Match, you could've just said so.

192
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,660
Why all the sneaking around?

193
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:26,460
Fatty, I think the way you'll look when you cry later

194
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,820
is going to be really funny.

195
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,700
Hmph! We'll see who's crying. Let's go.

196
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:46,620
Hey, aren't you hot wearing that mask all day?

197
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,660
What's it to you?

198
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:49,980
Just make your move.

199
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:52,300
Then I'll show you what I've got first.

200
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,000
[Name: Marco | Title: Yo-Yo Maverick]
[Yo-Yo: Speed Demon | Special Move: Thousand Dragons Rising]

201
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:40,000
[Name: Chuck | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Nuclear Fission | Special Move: Lunar Core Fission]

202
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:41,340
Watch this.

203
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:13,020
Well?

204
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:14,940
Now you see Chuck's not just average, right?

205
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,340
From what I know,

206
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:22,620
you're nothing but bottom-tier on Jianghai Team.

207
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:26,460
What? Then I'll show you my Ultimate Move!

208
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,740
Lunar Core Fission!

209
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,580
Thousand Dragons Rising!

210
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:55,760
My Yo-Yo!

211
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,700
Is this the place?

212
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:45,660
Yeah, right here.

213
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:47,580
Captain, look.

214
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,820
Mark, come to the bamboo grove tomorrow.

215
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:55,740
Come alone.

216
00:19:56,200 --> 00:20:00,540
Otherwise, Chuck's Yo-Yo will disappear forever!

217
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:14,460
Who could this mystery guy be?

218
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,260
It's gotta be someone from Chengnan Team.

219
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,960
And he managed to snatch Chuck's Yo-Yo just like that.

220
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,500
His skills must be serious.

221
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,900
Way above Jacky's level.

222
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:32,220
There's no way Chengnan Team has a Player that good.

223
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,380
So where'd he come from?

224
00:20:37,090 --> 00:20:39,920
I've been thinking about it, and it just doesn't add up.

225
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,300
If he was just some Random Pro passing by,

226
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,660
he wouldn't know our Team's situation that well.

227
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,150
He's definitely here targeting us on purpose.

228
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:54,780
He said that trick was called
"Feint East, Strike West."

229
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:59,100
Wow, that sounds intense.

230
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,420
He's using variations of Twin Dragons Rising.

231
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,780
Seems like his specialty is dual-handed play.

232
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,380
Captain, what did he say in his letter?

233
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,780
I'll handle it.

234
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:20,820
Don't worry about it.

